{
  "_note": "Maps each SAM 3 text prompt to the Carbon type(s) it can produce, in order of preference. SAM 3 finds shapes for a phrase, not Carbon types, so some components are derived: Tile (card) comes from 'rectangle' and 'white rectangle'; Tag comes from 'button' and is told apart from Button by height; NumberInput, TextArea and TextInput are derived from 'horizontal line' plus 'down arrow', 'plus sign' and 'minus sign'; Tab is derived from 'grey tab' plus 'horizontal line'. A type starting with an underscore is HELPER evidence that normalize_detections.py uses and never outputs. 'geometry' gates each type by size in design px: a hit that fits none of its types is dropped, not guessed. Carbon heights: Button 32/40/48/64/80, Tag 18/24, Field 40.",
  "prompts": [
    {"prompt": "rectangle", "types": ["Tile"]},
    {"prompt": "white rectangle", "types": ["Tile"]},
    {"prompt": "button", "types": ["Button", "Tag"]},
    {"prompt": "dropdown menu", "types": ["Dropdown"]},
    {"prompt": "text input field", "types": ["TextInput", "Dropdown"]},
    {"prompt": "checkbox", "types": ["Checkbox"]},
    {"prompt": "icon", "types": ["Icon"]},
    {"prompt": "horizontal line", "types": ["_Line"]},
    {"prompt": "grey tab", "types": ["_TabStrip"]},
    {"prompt": "down arrow", "types": ["_Chevron"]},
    {"prompt": "plus sign", "types": ["_Plus"]},
    {"prompt": "minus sign", "types": ["_Minus"]},

    {"prompt": "card", "types": ["Tile"]},
    {"prompt": "tag", "types": ["Tag"]},
    {"prompt": "link", "types": ["Link"]},
    {"prompt": "heading text", "types": ["Heading"]},
    {"prompt": "section", "types": ["Region"]},
    {"prompt": "panel", "types": ["Region"]},
    {"prompt": "tab bar", "types": ["Tabs"]},

    {"prompt": "toggle switch", "types": ["Toggle"]},
    {"prompt": "radio button", "types": ["RadioButton"]},
    {"prompt": "data table", "types": ["DataTable"]},
    {"prompt": "header bar", "types": ["Header"]},
    {"prompt": "side navigation", "types": ["SideNav"]},
    {"prompt": "modal dialog", "types": ["Modal"]},
